From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:10:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] ASoC: qcom: q6apm: add out-of-band APM SET_CFG

A SET_CFG packet larger than the ADSP glink intents (about 2.2 kB)
cannot be sent in band. Add q6apm_set_cfg_oob() which, as Qualcomm's
GSL does, copies the records to 4 KiB-aligned pages on the q6apm-dai
device (the one behind the ADSP IOMMU), maps them with
APM_CMD_SHARED_MEM_MAP_REGIONS, sends APM_CMD_SET_CFG by address,
checks the per-record errors and unmaps. A config map token bit keeps
its answers away from the PCM map handles.

A buffer whose map or unmap outcome is unknown may still be mapped by
the DSP, so it is leaked rather than freed. Out-of-band SET_CFG is
unavailable when q6apm-dai memory is SCM-assigned.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.h |   1 +
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c  |  15 ++
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c      | 230 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.h      |   9 ++
 4 files changed, 253 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

