From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:10:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] ASoC: qcom: q6apm: release out-of-band SET_CFG buffers the
 DSP let go

An out-of-band SET_CFG buffer whose map or unmap outcome is unknown is
leaked for good, although the DSP may answer the map late, a later
unmap may succeed, and a DSP restart drops every mapping.

Keep such buffers on a quarantine list tagged with the DSP session that
mapped them. A late map answer, matched by its token, records the
handle; the next out-of-band SET_CFG first unmaps the current session's
quarantined buffers and frees those the DSP acknowledges, and an lpass
shutdown frees them without unmapping. Buffers left at module removal
are leaked, so the APM and q6apm-dai get suppress_bind_attrs: their
removal does not prove the DSP stopped using a buffer.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
